1
00:00:00,560 --> 00:00:01,840
O, my friend!

2
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:04,440
This is a victory for us!

3
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:07,600
Our fame starts here!

4
00:00:07,640 --> 00:00:08,600
O, my friend!

5
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:13,900
Let us celebrate this victory
for the next battle!

6
00:00:28,540 --> 00:00:34,080
"I died for naught" I won't
let it end like that for you

7
00:00:34,080 --> 00:00:39,340
until I am the last one standing

8
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:42,320
The enemy is cruel... We will kill

9
00:00:42,320 --> 00:00:45,360
The enemy is colossal... We will jump

10
00:00:45,360 --> 00:00:49,000
In our hands we hold blades of glory

11
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,280
and sing in the name of victory

12
00:00:51,280 --> 00:00:55,920
We bear the wings of freedom on our backs

13
00:00:57,240 --> 00:01:03,360
Swearing iron determination upon our hearts,

14
00:01:03,380 --> 00:01:07,900
we slash apart the circle of idiocy

15
00:01:09,480 --> 00:01:11,800
and soar through the sky

16
00:01:11,860 --> 00:01:16,060
with our wings of freedom

17
00:01:29,980 --> 00:01:34,990
Smile: Assault on Stohess, Part 1

18
00:01:37,540 --> 00:01:39,160
Keep it up, Annie!

19
00:01:41,980 --> 00:01:44,260
That's my daughter!

20
00:01:46,130 --> 00:01:48,580
What are you doing? Don't stop!

21
00:02:03,790 --> 00:02:05,740
Wall Sina
Eastern Wall City

22
00:02:05,740 --> 00:02:06,870
Huh? Didn't you hear?

23
00:02:06,870 --> 00:02:11,020
The Titan boy and his companions
were summoned by the King.

24
00:02:11,210 --> 00:02:13,410
They'll be passing through the city today.

25
00:02:13,410 --> 00:02:14,460
I see.

26
00:02:14,460 --> 00:02:17,530
He's gonna wind up getting
dissected for sure this time.

27
00:02:17,530 --> 00:02:23,530
Either way, I just hope things work
out so they'll seal the gates.

28
00:02:24,540 --> 00:02:28,220
What?! Did you just say "seal the gates"?

29
00:02:28,220 --> 00:02:32,080
Do you want to further defile our
gods with lowly human meddling?!

30
00:02:33,580 --> 00:02:37,090
Maria! Rose! Sina!

31
00:02:37,090 --> 00:02:41,980
How dare you even suggest desecrating
our three sacred goddesses?!

32
00:02:41,980 --> 00:02:44,720
He's one of those crazies who
worship the Walls as gods.

33
00:02:44,720 --> 00:02:45,630
Just ignore him.

34
00:02:45,630 --> 00:02:48,700
Indeed... Those freaks still exist...

35
00:02:48,700 --> 00:02:50,230
Damn it.
It's the Walls! The Walls and
nothing else are our protectors!

36
00:02:50,230 --> 00:02:55,000
It's the Walls! The Walls and
nothing else are our protectors!

37
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:55,080
Stohess Military Police Branch
It's the Walls! The Walls and
nothing else are our protectors!

38
00:02:55,080 --> 00:02:58,390
Stohess Military Police Branch

39
00:03:00,910 --> 00:03:03,160
You're finally up.

40
00:03:03,160 --> 00:03:07,160
You looked so scary in your sleep
nobody dared to wake you up.

41
00:03:07,160 --> 00:03:09,400
Sorry, Annie.

42
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:11,420
You've been slacking off a lot recently.

43
00:03:12,070 --> 00:03:15,800
What? Are you mad?

44
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:17,670
How are we supposed to get along?

45
00:03:17,670 --> 00:03:22,280
Leave her be. She's from Trost, remember.

46
00:03:22,280 --> 00:03:25,190
She's the only person in this branch
with any actual combat experience.

47
00:03:25,190 --> 00:03:29,190
Of course she can't smile cheerfully
when she's just returned from hell.

48
00:03:29,430 --> 00:03:34,560
Oh, I get it. So you like her?

49
00:03:34,560 --> 00:03:36,460
I wonder what you see in her.

50
00:03:36,460 --> 00:03:42,040
Hitch... There's only one way a dimwitted
chick like you gets into the Military Police.

51
00:03:42,420 --> 00:03:45,740
What's that? I wouldn't know.

52
00:03:45,770 --> 00:03:46,660
Tell me?

53
00:03:46,660 --> 00:03:47,850
Shut up, you two.

54
00:03:52,830 --> 00:03:54,860
Don't bother.

55
00:03:55,570 --> 00:03:59,260
Today you'll be doing something
other than your usual chores.

56
00:03:59,260 --> 00:04:00,860
That's why I ordered you to assemble here.

57
00:04:01,380 --> 00:04:05,130
A unit from the Recon Corps has
been summoned by the King.

58
00:04:05,540 --> 00:04:09,370
They're passing through the
city's main street today.

59
00:04:10,030 --> 00:04:12,910
Escorting them to the capitol is
Military Police HQ's responsibility,

60
00:04:12,910 --> 00:04:15,880
so we only need to accompany
them as they pass through town.

61
00:04:16,430 --> 00:04:19,860
The use of 3D Maneuver Gear will be
temporarily permitted within city limits.

62
00:04:19,860 --> 00:04:23,390
You will guard the convoy in
tandem with their own security.

63
00:04:23,390 --> 00:04:28,260
You'll travel by barge to
the mission starting point.

64
00:04:28,780 --> 00:04:30,680
May I ask a question?

65
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:32,420
What?

66
00:04:32,420 --> 00:04:35,650
What are we protecting the convoy from?

67
00:04:38,510 --> 00:04:42,860
I'm unaware of any people within
this Wall who'd oppose the King.

68
00:04:43,240 --> 00:04:45,480
Even if we've overlooked some petty criminals,

69
00:04:45,480 --> 00:04:48,490
truly organized opposition
would be unimaginable,

70
00:04:48,510 --> 00:04:51,310
unless they had a stronghold
outside the Wall.

71
00:04:51,310 --> 00:04:53,140
Why would anyone even try such
a thing in the first place?

72
00:04:53,140 --> 00:04:55,520
Oh, well aren't you clever?

73
00:04:55,520 --> 00:04:57,340
I'm putting you in charge.

74
00:04:57,340 --> 00:05:00,010
The details are all here.

75
00:05:03,180 --> 00:05:08,460
We officers are really busy. You
can handle this yourselves.

76
00:05:09,680 --> 00:05:12,190
Just don't screw it up.

77
00:05:12,890 --> 00:05:15,200
Sorry for the wait, guys. Where were we?

78
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:16,780
Whose turn is it?

79
00:05:21,920 --> 00:05:23,950
Those damn bastards!

80
00:05:23,950 --> 00:05:29,180
Yeah... The Military Police are
even more rotten than I imagined.

81
00:05:29,180 --> 00:05:32,280
That's why I picked being an MP, but still...

82
00:05:32,280 --> 00:05:36,740
They force us rookies to handle everything.

83
00:05:36,740 --> 00:05:39,120
I didn't expect that.

84
00:05:39,120 --> 00:05:43,180
Scumbags. They can't think
of anything but themselves.

85
00:05:43,180 --> 00:05:44,220
Fucking scumbags.

86
00:05:44,960 --> 00:05:47,220
What are you talking about, Marlo?

87
00:05:47,220 --> 00:05:50,600
You joined the Police too. You're no better.

88
00:05:52,740 --> 00:05:56,150
I'm not the same. I'm not scum like you guys.

89
00:05:56,900 --> 00:06:00,360
I came here to correct the Military Police!

90
00:06:02,840 --> 00:06:07,070
Impressive, Marlo! So that's how you roll?

91
00:06:07,070 --> 00:06:08,910
And how will you fix things?

92
00:06:09,310 --> 00:06:11,870
I'll have to work my way to the top.

93
00:06:11,870 --> 00:06:18,200
When I'm in charge, I will enforce
the rules and punish corruption.

94
00:06:18,200 --> 00:06:19,250
It's that simple.

95
00:06:20,300 --> 00:06:23,420
I'll make the Police a place
for normal people again.

96
00:06:23,420 --> 00:06:24,300
That's all.

97
00:06:24,950 --> 00:06:27,370
The way humans are meant to be!

98
00:06:29,120 --> 00:06:32,170
Holy shit, you're the real deal!

99
00:06:32,170 --> 00:06:35,560
Here I thought you were a total bore!
So sorry!

100
00:06:36,340 --> 00:06:40,880
What a noble goal you have. Do your best.

101
00:06:40,880 --> 00:06:42,040
I wonder.

102
00:06:43,030 --> 00:06:46,640
If a "good person" like you
controlled the system,

103
00:06:46,640 --> 00:06:48,820
that'd be the end for us, I think.

104
00:06:48,820 --> 00:06:52,080
What? You can actually speak?

105
00:06:52,850 --> 00:06:55,620
I think you're right.

106
00:06:56,010 --> 00:06:57,760
You say all the correct things.

107
00:06:58,400 --> 00:07:00,840
I know another person much like you.

108
00:07:01,890 --> 00:07:06,680
You need a lot of courage to
go against the greater flow.

109
00:07:06,680 --> 00:07:08,080
I can respect that.

110
00:07:09,050 --> 00:07:12,080
But that doesn't mean you're not an idiot.

111
00:07:12,870 --> 00:07:15,560
Maybe it's just that the other
person you know is an idiot.

112
00:07:15,740 --> 00:07:17,310
I'm different from him!

113
00:07:19,410 --> 00:07:21,180
We've wasted too much time talking.

114
00:07:21,180 --> 00:07:22,220
Let's move out!

115
00:07:28,240 --> 00:07:31,870
The convoy will pass through
the outer gate in 45 minutes.

116
00:07:31,870 --> 00:07:35,910
Once we're there, everyone confirm
your designated positions.

117
00:07:35,910 --> 00:07:36,720
Got it?

118
00:07:36,720 --> 00:07:38,330
Yeah, yeah.

119
00:07:42,820 --> 00:07:44,380
Hey!

120
00:07:45,660 --> 00:07:46,880
What's going on?

121
00:07:47,250 --> 00:07:49,090
Aren't those ours?

122
00:07:49,290 --> 00:07:50,940
They must be taking them
to the Inner District.

123
00:07:50,940 --> 00:07:54,350
Even so, having the merchants
involved is unusual.

124
00:07:55,460 --> 00:07:57,540
What are they up to?

125
00:08:05,280 --> 00:08:08,280
They're selling our emergency backups?!

126
00:08:10,520 --> 00:08:12,810
Wait, what about the mission?

127
00:08:12,810 --> 00:08:16,030
Holy shit, he really is the real deal!

128
00:08:16,030 --> 00:08:18,760
Guess we'll see if that's
for better or for worse...

129
00:08:18,760 --> 00:08:20,540
For now let's just enjoy the show.

130
00:08:28,190 --> 00:08:30,620
Let's grab a drink then.

131
00:08:33,460 --> 00:08:36,360
What is it, rookie? What do you want?

132
00:08:36,360 --> 00:08:40,890
E-Embezzling emergency
backup supplies is a crime!

133
00:08:41,780 --> 00:08:42,690
So?

134
00:08:44,460 --> 00:08:49,900
Emergency goods are paid for by
the people's tax dollars and...

135
00:08:51,660 --> 00:08:55,530
So you think you can lecture
your superiors, rookie?

136
00:08:55,800 --> 00:08:59,120
I look forward to your future.

137
00:09:01,330 --> 00:09:04,310
For now, go buy yourself a
hooker and chill the fuck out.

138
00:09:06,360 --> 00:09:08,240
H-Hold it!

139
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:11,010
Embezzling is...

140
00:09:34,090 --> 00:09:35,120
Hey!

141
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:41,540
I'll have you arrested for
insubordination and treason.

142
00:09:42,110 --> 00:09:44,630
Damn you! You can't get away...

143
00:09:44,630 --> 00:09:45,920
Yes, we can.

144
00:09:46,790 --> 00:09:48,210
Here, we can!

145
00:09:51,010 --> 00:09:53,550
I think that's probably enough.

146
00:09:56,040 --> 00:10:00,560
Sorry if this retard was causing you trouble.

147
00:10:01,140 --> 00:10:04,580
We'll be sure he learns his lesson.

148
00:10:04,580 --> 00:10:06,150
Unless...

149
00:10:07,030 --> 00:10:10,980
You'd prefer to make a bigger scene?

150
00:10:14,060 --> 00:10:15,980
We'll let you off this once.

151
00:10:15,980 --> 00:10:16,880
Yes, sir!

152
00:10:20,100 --> 00:10:22,320
Let's go grab that drink now.

153
00:10:22,320 --> 00:10:24,750
Why not do it?

154
00:10:36,370 --> 00:10:43,980
Weren't you going to punish corruption?

155
00:10:44,840 --> 00:10:48,260
If you want, I'll help out.

156
00:10:53,900 --> 00:10:54,860
What did you wanna get?

157
00:10:54,860 --> 00:10:55,900
What else?

158
00:10:56,080 --> 00:10:57,210
Meat!

159
00:11:00,990 --> 00:11:01,990
Damn it!

160
00:11:04,050 --> 00:11:07,880
We know you're working really hard!

161
00:11:07,880 --> 00:11:10,540
Oh, I'm not worthy of your praise.

162
00:11:13,440 --> 00:11:15,470
That guy you know...

163
00:11:16,700 --> 00:11:19,170
That idiot you mentioned earlier...

164
00:11:19,170 --> 00:11:20,300
Would he have done it?

165
00:11:23,520 --> 00:11:24,720
Maybe.

166
00:11:29,320 --> 00:11:36,720
Then I'm just another piece of trash, caught
up in that greater flow you mentioned earlier.

167
00:11:36,720 --> 00:11:38,100
Am I not?

168
00:11:38,960 --> 00:11:40,740
Who knows?

169
00:11:42,280 --> 00:11:46,250
But isn't that what normal human beings do?

170
00:11:47,840 --> 00:11:56,480
I don't care if I'm swept along by the flow,
as long as I'm still considered a human.

171
00:12:20,520 --> 00:12:21,480
Annie!

172
00:12:33,920 --> 00:12:34,880
Hey.

173
00:12:35,260 --> 00:12:38,380
You're fitting in well
with the Military Police.

174
00:12:40,260 --> 00:12:41,480
Armin...

175
00:12:54,520 --> 00:12:57,190
What's with that look?

176
00:12:57,190 --> 00:12:59,470
I disguised myself as a porter.

177
00:12:59,470 --> 00:13:03,370
The cloak can hide my 3D Maneuver Gear.

178
00:13:03,970 --> 00:13:05,000
See?

179
00:13:06,060 --> 00:13:07,700
What's going on?

180
00:13:08,480 --> 00:13:13,170
Annie, would you assist
me in letting Eren escape?

181
00:13:13,340 --> 00:13:15,300
Escape to where?

182
00:13:15,300 --> 00:13:19,740
Where could you go inside these
Walls after disobeying the King?

183
00:13:19,740 --> 00:13:22,320
We'd just hide out for a while.

184
00:13:22,320 --> 00:13:25,090
We don't intend to go
against the King head-on.

185
00:13:25,390 --> 00:13:29,500
It'll be reported as a rebellion
by a portion of the Recon Corps.

186
00:13:29,500 --> 00:13:30,990
We need to buy time.

187
00:13:31,010 --> 00:13:35,450
Time to collect proof that could change
the outcome of the court martial.

188
00:13:35,450 --> 00:13:36,730
We will succeed.

189
00:13:37,270 --> 00:13:39,840
Change the outcome?

190
00:13:39,840 --> 00:13:42,250
Does anything so convenient even exist?

191
00:13:42,610 --> 00:13:43,570
What's your evidence?

192
00:13:46,140 --> 00:13:48,120
Sorry, but I can't say.

193
00:13:51,040 --> 00:13:54,040
I'm sorry too, but I can't help you like this.

194
00:13:54,220 --> 00:13:57,320
Good luck with whatever you're doing.

195
00:13:58,470 --> 00:14:01,060
Annie! Please!

196
00:14:01,060 --> 00:14:02,800
They're gonna wind up executing Eren!

197
00:14:04,800 --> 00:14:10,040
Clueless people will push mankind
down the path of extinction

198
00:14:10,040 --> 00:14:13,160
just for personal gain,
without even realizing it!

199
00:14:13,160 --> 00:14:15,880
I know my reasoning isn't all that convincing.

200
00:14:16,310 --> 00:14:17,820
But even so...

201
00:14:17,820 --> 00:14:20,560
Gambling big is our only chance at this point!

202
00:14:21,820 --> 00:14:25,760
Of course, we'll do our utmost to
avoid causing trouble for you.

203
00:14:25,760 --> 00:14:29,680
But to get through the
security inside Wall Sina,

204
00:14:29,680 --> 00:14:32,330
we need insider help from the Military Police.

205
00:14:33,590 --> 00:14:34,980
We have no other choice.

206
00:14:36,510 --> 00:14:41,340
Do I look like such a good person to you?

207
00:14:42,070 --> 00:14:43,600
"Good person"?

208
00:14:43,600 --> 00:14:49,350
Well... I don't like that term.

209
00:14:49,520 --> 00:14:56,500
To me, it seems like the meaning of "good
person" is really a person who's good for you.

210
00:14:57,100 --> 00:15:01,610
In that sense, I don't think any individual
can be "good" in everyone's eyes.

211
00:15:01,610 --> 00:15:05,750
So if you don't help us...

212
00:15:07,110 --> 00:15:10,620
Then, in my eyes, you'd be a bad person.

213
00:15:28,160 --> 00:15:29,140
Very well.

214
00:15:35,730 --> 00:15:37,050
I'm in.

215
00:15:48,850 --> 00:15:52,330
We made it through more
easily than I expected.

216
00:15:52,330 --> 00:15:56,860
That's the Military Police for you.
You can tell how hard they work.

217
00:15:56,860 --> 00:15:58,330
Stop glancing around so much.

218
00:15:58,740 --> 00:16:02,060
Let's just hope they don't
discover Jean's taken my place.

219
00:16:02,060 --> 00:16:04,300
I doubt that cover will last long.

220
00:16:04,920 --> 00:16:08,170
We look nothing alike.

221
00:16:08,390 --> 00:16:10,070
Don't worry.

222
00:16:10,070 --> 00:16:13,930
You both share a villainous face and
a sociopathic look in your eyes.

223
00:16:14,150 --> 00:16:16,330
I don't have a horseface like him!

224
00:16:16,330 --> 00:16:21,810
Hey, if I didn't agree to help, how
were you planning to get over the Wall?

225
00:16:22,180 --> 00:16:25,070
I was going to use the 3D
Maneuver Gear to break through.

226
00:16:25,240 --> 00:16:26,840
That's insane.

227
00:16:26,840 --> 00:16:32,820
Wouldn't it have been less troublesome
to escape before you reached Stohess?

228
00:16:33,190 --> 00:16:35,840
Why here? Why now?

229
00:16:35,840 --> 00:16:38,020
I thought the dense layout of the urban area

230
00:16:38,020 --> 00:16:41,830
would give us a better shot
at swapping Jean for Eren.

231
00:16:41,830 --> 00:16:47,010
Plus, pretending to follow
obediently instead of opposing them

232
00:16:47,040 --> 00:16:50,330
outright will buy us
more time to flee.

233
00:16:51,560 --> 00:16:54,750
I see. That makes sense.

234
00:16:59,250 --> 00:17:00,460
There!

235
00:17:09,400 --> 00:17:10,730
Here?

236
00:17:10,730 --> 00:17:13,050
Yeah. We'll go through here.

237
00:17:13,490 --> 00:17:17,640
It's the abandoned remains of an
underground city they planned long ago.

238
00:17:19,880 --> 00:17:23,870
This leads as far as the outer gate.

239
00:17:23,870 --> 00:17:26,040
Really? That's great!

240
00:17:27,640 --> 00:17:28,750
Annie?

241
00:17:29,260 --> 00:17:34,390
What's wrong? Don't tell me you're
scared of cramped, dark places?

242
00:17:35,360 --> 00:17:37,930
In fact, I am afraid.

243
00:17:38,520 --> 00:17:42,570
I doubt a brave, borderline-suicidal
guy like you could possibly

244
00:17:42,600 --> 00:17:45,720
understand the feelings
of a weak maiden like me.

245
00:17:49,110 --> 00:17:54,240
Someone who can fling a man head over heels in
mid-air with ease can't call herself a maiden.

246
00:17:54,240 --> 00:17:56,200
Stop being silly and hurry up!

247
00:17:56,200 --> 00:17:58,450
No, I'm not going that way.

248
00:17:59,870 --> 00:18:01,930
It scares me.

249
00:18:01,930 --> 00:18:04,870
If we don't travel above ground, I won't help.

250
00:18:15,300 --> 00:18:16,840
What are you even saying?!

251
00:18:16,840 --> 00:18:19,560
Get down here already! Stop screwing around!

252
00:18:19,560 --> 00:18:20,960
Eren, don't shout.

253
00:18:20,960 --> 00:18:23,090
It shouldn't be an issue, right, Mikasa?

254
00:18:24,310 --> 00:18:30,820
For some reason, there haven't been
any people nearby for a while now.

255
00:18:38,640 --> 00:18:41,660
Jeez! I'm hurt.

256
00:18:44,370 --> 00:18:51,610
When did you start looking at
me with those eyes, Armin?

257
00:18:53,040 --> 00:18:55,220
Annie, why?

258
00:18:56,120 --> 00:18:59,300
Why did you have Marco's 3D Maneuver Gear?

259
00:19:04,080 --> 00:19:06,860
I recognized even its tiniest marks and dings

260
00:19:06,860 --> 00:19:09,190
because we repaired ours together.

261
00:19:09,990 --> 00:19:11,980
That's how I knew.

262
00:19:12,360 --> 00:19:13,370
I see...

263
00:19:14,440 --> 00:19:17,610
Well, I happened to pick it up.

264
00:19:19,740 --> 00:19:25,380
Then you killed those two
Titans we captured alive?

265
00:19:25,380 --> 00:19:26,810
Who knows?

266
00:19:27,450 --> 00:19:32,530
But if you thought so a month
ago, why didn't you act?

267
00:19:32,530 --> 00:19:35,210
Because I couldn't believe it!

268
00:19:35,210 --> 00:19:40,470
I still hope it's just some misunderstanding!

269
00:19:41,940 --> 00:19:44,430
But because of that...

270
00:19:45,720 --> 00:19:49,650
Since you... didn't kill me back then...

271
00:19:49,900 --> 00:19:54,150
That's why this is happening right now.

272
00:20:02,100 --> 00:20:05,140
Yeah, I'm pretty sure you're right.

273
00:20:06,180 --> 00:20:10,280
I never expected you to corner me like this.

274
00:20:13,040 --> 00:20:18,340
Why didn't I kill you then? I wonder.

275
00:20:19,090 --> 00:20:20,770
Hey, Annie!

276
00:20:20,770 --> 00:20:23,760
There's still a chance that you've
just got a sick sense of humor,

277
00:20:23,760 --> 00:20:28,170
and you're just going along with whatever
Armin says because you're an idiot.

278
00:20:28,170 --> 00:20:30,060
So get down here now!

279
00:20:31,060 --> 00:20:34,180
If you come underground,
that alone proves something!

280
00:20:34,180 --> 00:20:35,980
Come on and prove it!

281
00:20:36,900 --> 00:20:38,690
I can't go down there...

282
00:20:38,690 --> 00:20:41,740
I've failed to become a soldier.

283
00:20:41,740 --> 00:20:44,700
Cut it out already!

284
00:20:44,700 --> 00:20:46,200
Tell us, Annie!

285
00:20:46,200 --> 00:20:48,120
We can still talk...

286
00:20:48,120 --> 00:20:49,530
That's enough.

287
00:20:50,150 --> 00:20:51,920
I can't listen to another word of this.

288
00:20:53,220 --> 00:20:54,510
It's pointless.

289
00:20:56,460 --> 00:20:59,050
I'll tear you apart once again,

290
00:20:59,050 --> 00:21:01,280
female-form Titan!

291
00:21:27,540 --> 00:21:29,130
Armin,

292
00:21:29,130 --> 00:21:32,470
I'm glad I could be a good person for you.

293
00:21:33,370 --> 00:21:35,910
You've won your bet.

294
00:21:38,450 --> 00:21:43,550
But this is where my gamble begins!

295
00:21:56,920 --> 00:21:58,090
Eren!

296
00:22:03,920 --> 00:22:04,740
Mikasa!

297
00:22:04,740 --> 00:22:05,820
We were too late!

298
00:22:36,200 --> 00:22:41,590
If we suppose that I am not me,

299
00:22:41,590 --> 00:22:46,130
Can you say with certainty that you are you?

300
00:22:46,780 --> 00:22:51,660
Will you be able to pick up after yourself

301
00:22:51,660 --> 00:22:56,810
Once your sand-like shell breaks and your heart crumbles?

302
00:22:57,090 --> 00:23:02,020
I could hear someone calling

303
00:23:02,310 --> 00:23:05,920
But now my ears are just ringing

304
00:23:06,240 --> 00:23:11,080
It's as if time has frozen

305
00:23:11,380 --> 00:23:13,990
Now, wake up

306
00:23:13,990 --> 00:23:18,960
I began to walk through a deep dark abyss

307
00:23:19,510 --> 00:23:24,260
As swift as a gale, I escaped for my life

308
00:23:24,670 --> 00:23:28,830
I felt like a living corpse

309
00:23:29,240 --> 00:23:33,960
We break out of our walls

310
00:23:34,270 --> 00:23:40,350
To reunite in worlds we've yet to map

311
00:23:53,288 --> 00:23:57,311
The Female Titan was Annie Leonhart.

312
00:23:58,133 --> 00:24:02,170
Eren is unable to transform in face of the Female Titan.

313
00:24:03,111 --> 00:24:05,215
because he knows it to be Annie.

314
00:24:05,215 --> 00:24:05,911
Mercy: Assault on Stohess, Part 2
because he knows it to be Annie.

315
00:24:05,911 --> 00:24:06,966
Mercy: Assault on Stohess, Part 2
